From f8a28129df26011ee69515a7fe77a8d0cb324d66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: testuser <mainta@example.test>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 02:12:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] fix(llms): send GLM 5.3 on Bedrock Converse its
 reasoning_effort

- Match only us.zai.glm-5.3, global.zai.glm-5.3 and zai.glm-5.3 on Bedrock.
  Reject padded ids and other geo prefixes. Leave other GLM routes unchanged.
- Send levels through additionalModelRequestFields.reasoning_effort, Bedrock's native reasoning field,
  in the ConverseStream body.
- Keep explicit low, medium, high, xhigh and max levels.
  Map minimal, reasoning off and no reasoning request to low.
  Use medium when reasoning is enabled without a level.
- Pass requestedReasoning, the caller's fitted reasoning, before removing portable levels.
- Count the nested reasoning_effort key as a native reasoning control.
  Ignore other container fields. Prevent duplicate levels and "The feature reasoning is not supported".
- Keep catalog overrides outside catalog.generated.ts so regeneration preserves them.
  Offer low, medium, high, xhigh and max without an off switch.
- Bedrock ignored the old top-level reasoning object.
  A three-file task used 13,006 output tokens and 183 seconds.
  Live checks measured 856 output tokens without a level against 159 at low.
- routing/bedrock-glm-effort.test.ts covers 25 rule cases.
  vendors/bedrock-glm-reasoning.wire.test.ts checks the real adapter's body.
  catalog/catalog-overrides.test.ts checks the catalog overrides.
